      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14253566/assets/2b7e93b99c5ff7cc66a8d012e8c2ba6f828228bd8ea4e17f838723f8f9c91ae6.png)\n\nThe shaded region above represents the truth set of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following is the truth set of $¬P(x).$",
      "worked_solution": "The truth set of $¬P(x)$ is the *complement* of the truth set of $P(x):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{¬P}={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\n$$\n\nTherefore, to get the truth set of $¬P(x),$ we take all the points that belong to $U$ and do not lie in ${T}_{p},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14253566/assets/c5534ee4c3d936431b2fc51c5f906838671552f615629cd05882917064f7ad0d.png)",
